    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "True or False? Let $A$ and $B$ be sets in a universal set $U$.\n\n$\\overline{A\\cup B}=\\overline A\\cup\\overline B$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "False.",
      "worked": "False. Let $U=\\{1,2\\}$, $A=\\{1\\}$ and $B=\\{2\\}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\overline{A\\cup B}&=\\overline{\\{1,2\\}},\\\\\\overline{A\\cup B}&=\\varnothing,\\\\\\overline A\\cup\\overline B&=\\{2\\}\\cup\\{1\\},\\\\\\overline A\\cup\\overline B&=\\{1,2\\}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe two sets differ.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
